<title>FINLAND: Finnish prelim June trade surplus FIM 2.8 bln -NCB.</title>
<headline>Finnish prelim June trade surplus FIM 2.8 bln -NCB.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-08-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finland's preliminary trade surplus fell to 2.8 billion markka in June from 4.67 billion in May and from 5.50 billion in June last year, the National Customs Board (NCB) said in statement on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The value of exports fell seven percent year-on-year in June and the value of imports rose 13 percent, NCB said. @</p>
<p>Preliminary trade balance (million markka):</p>
<p>		 June '97    May '97   June '96</p>
<p> Exports	 16,000     16,657     17,158</p>
<p> Imports	 13,200     11,989     11,659</p>
<p> Balance	 +2,800     +4,668     +5,499</p>
<p>The mean of six economists' forecasts for the June trade balance had been for a 4.4 billion markka surplus (range 3.5-5.5 bln).</p>
<p>-- Helsinki newsroom +358-9-680 50 245, news@reuters.fi</p>
